# AMDA /admin — server-side password gate (layer 2 of admin security).
# Layer 1 (build credentials via `npm run admin:hash`) is already in the code.
# This file enforces a REAL server login before the admin page even loads.
#
# ACTIVATE (pick one):
#   A) Easiest — cPanel "Directory Privacy": select the `admin` folder, enable
#      protection, create a user. cPanel writes its own block here; keep this file.
#   B) Manual — create the password file OUTSIDE the web root, e.g.:
#        htpasswd -c /home/YOURUSER/.htpasswds/amda-admin editor-name
#      then uncomment the 4 lines below and fix the AuthUserFile path:
#
# AuthType Basic
# AuthName "AMDA Admin — authorized editors only"
# AuthUserFile /home/YOURUSER/.htpasswds/amda-admin
# Require valid-user
#
# NEVER put the .htpasswd file inside the site folder — it would be downloadable.
# Until activated, this file does nothing (block above stays commented).
